<code>assert \old(this.get(index)).equals(\result);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.get(index)).equals(\result);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.get(index)).equals(\result);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.get(index)).equals(\result);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.get(index).equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>

However, since we need to refer to the previous value before the set operation, the correct assert statement should use the returned value from the set method:

<code>assert \result.equals(\old(this.get(index)));</code>
--------------------
